# e2e/w87a-punch.spec.ts — a creature's blow on a player shakes, cracks and knocks the table as its landing would.
# bob (ai, seat 1) is the active player with four vanilla attackers already attacking alice (human, seat 0)
# at 30 life: Grizzly Bears (2), Spined Wurm (5), Pelakka Wurm (7) and Ancient Brontodon (9), one charge per
# rung of `entries.ts`'s `entryWeight` (nothing at 2, the shake from 5, cracks from 7, the cards around it
# knocked away from 8). 23 damage, so alice lives and every blow is drawn. alice's Grizzly Bears are what a
# heavy blow knocks away; she declares no blocks. The attackers stand out of order of power (9, 2, 7, 5): their
# blows still land weakest first, the 9 last.
# `activephase` lands on Declare ATTACKERS Step, as `cp-lethal-ram.state` does and for its reason; bob holds a
# Lightning Bolt so each of his stops on the way to combat damage is kept for the spec to press.
turn=1
activeplayer=ai
activephase=COMBAT_DECLARE_ATTACKERS
humanlife=30
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Mountain;Grizzly Bears;Grizzly Bears;Grizzly Bears;Grizzly Bears
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=Lightning Bolt
aibattlefield=Ancient Brontodon|Attacking;Grizzly Bears|Attacking;Pelakka Wurm|Attacking;Spined Wurm|Attacking;Mountain
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
